   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT directing the study of the future implementation of fifth and future\ngeneration wireless network system technology in the state",
    "basePrintNo": "S1607",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1607-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "State Technology",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1607\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act directing the study of the future implementation of fifth and\nfuture generation wireless network system technology in the state\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nDirecting the study cf the future implementation and of fifth generation\nand future generation wireless systems Technology in the state\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 addrers the topic which will be studied\n\nSection 2 sets the date and tineframe for the resort\n\nSection 3 specifies which data and technologies will he evaluated\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, Internet connectivity and wireless network capacity are no\nlonaer luxuries-thev are necessities. In New York State, we have more\nwireless phones and devices than people-and in the future, the trend\nwill continue.\n\nAs technology advances with the Internet of things, where cars, devices\nand systems will communicate with humans, each other and, the network,\nour current network capacity is truly lackina.\n\nThe Empire State is anything but empire with regard to cur network\ncapacity. We must build cut our network to ensure optimal capacity for\nat least the next two generations of New Yorkers,\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017/18 S.7635 - Energy & Telecommunications\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nEffective immediately\n",
